# component: input-group
# decisions: DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-5, FOC-6
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-3, FOC-6: the group's `has-[[data-slot=input-group-control]:focus-visible]:border-ring`
#     plus `ring-3 ring-ring/50` becomes `has-[[data-slot=input-group-control]:focus]:border-ring/70`
#     — the text-entry border tint on the GROUP, on `:focus`, and no glow. Batch 4 added the same
#     tint for `[data-slot=command-input]`: upstream's `CommandInput` puts cmdk's input inside an
#     `InputGroup` but names its slot `command-input`, so the group never saw it focus and the one
#     text-entry affordance this system has went missing on the palette — caught by the geometry
#     lane's focus probe on all four command fixtures.
#   FOC-5: the invalid tint becomes
#     `not-focus-within:has-[[data-slot][aria-invalid=true]]:border-destructive`, so a focused group
#     shows its focus cue rather than the error colour; the `has-aria-invalid` halo rings go with it.
#   FOC-6: `InputGroupInput` and `InputGroupTextarea` drop `ring-0 focus-visible:ring-0
#     aria-invalid:ring-0`, which existed only to cancel the ring `Input` and `Textarea` no longer
#     have; `in-data-[slot=combobox-content]:focus-within:ring-0` goes for the same reason.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
